<title>USA: USAir Q3 undiluted shr rises to $0.69.</title>
<headline>USAir Q3 undiluted shr rises to $0.69.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON, Va. 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary	$0.69		    $0.35</p>
<p> Shr diluted	0.60		     n/a</p>
<p> Net		  67,738		   43,056</p>
<p> Revs		 2,073		    1,873</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary 65,838		   62,571</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted 95,754		   n/a</p>
<p>		     Nine months</p>
<p> Shr primary	$2.58	   loss   $(0.06)</p>
<p> Shr diluted	2.15		     n/a</p>
<p> Net		  236,220	 loss   (59,033)</p>
<p> Revs		 6,090		    5,620</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary 65,457		   62,143</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted 95,373		   n/a</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: First Call earnings estimate for the current quarter was $0.49 a share.  </p>
<p>Year-ago nine month period shows loss in parenthesis. Current and year-ago third quarter figures and current nine-month figures are profit figures.</p>
<p>Current third-quarter earnings include $41.1 million set aside to cover 1992 profit-sharing plan obligations. It also includes a $9.8 million expense to settle a lawsuit with travel agents over commissions.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
